        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Works: Father Was a Fullback, The Andy Griffith Show\n- People: Clifford Goldsmith, Fred MacMurray, Maureen O'Hara, Natalie Wood, Betty Lynn, Barney Fife, Thelma Lou\n- Companies: Twentieth Century Fox\n- Roles: Deputy Barney Fife's girlfriend\n\nFacts:\n- Father Was a Fullback is a 1949 black-and-white film produced by Twentieth Century Fox and based on a comedy by Clifford Goldsmith.\n- Father Was a Fullback stars Fred MacMurray, Maureen O'Hara, Natalie Wood, and Betty Lynn.\n- Betty Lynn is best known for playing Thelma Lou, who is Deputy Barney Fife's girlfriend, on The Andy Griffith Show.",
